27	// A MISSING maintenance.delivery is drift, not an error: the only writer is
28	// check_the_world --init (first adoption), so a repo adopted before the key existed
29	// — or one whose key was hand-removed — has nothing that could ever put it back,
30	// and a hard failure would just fail its tasks every night forever. Resolve the
31	// default instead (baselining is the one caller that also MATERIALIZES it). An
32	// UNRECOGNIZED value stays a hard failure: substituting a default there would
33	// deliver the opposite of a stated intent.
